Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 14:47:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix: profile photo upload, background notifications, and
 session persistence

Profile photo:
- Onboarding (ProfileSetup): re-enable the profile photo picker UI and append
  profile_image to the signup payload (was commented out / never sent).
- iOS upload (helpers): keep the file:// scheme so the picked image actually
  uploads instead of sending an empty file part.
- Edit Profile: only send profile_image when a new local file is picked; don't
  re-send the existing S3 URL as a file on an unchanged save.

Notifications (Issue A, frontend half):
- Move the FCM background/quit message handler to index.js (app entry point) so
  incoming session-request notifications fire even when the app is fully closed.
  Backend still needs to send a notification payload (not data-only) for iOS.

Session persistence (Issue B):
- Fix the 401 interceptor to refresh the token and retry instead of logging the
  interpreter out; only log out if the refresh itself fails. Refresh endpoint
  response fields (token/refresh_token) to be confirmed against the backend.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
